2. One paragraph is added as paragraph 2 to Article 166 of the Criminal Law, and that Article is amended to read: "Where a staff member of a State-owned company, enterprise, or institution, by taking advantage of his position, commits any of the following acts, thereby causing significant losses to the interests of the State, he shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years or criminal detention and shall also, or shall only, be fined; if he causes especially significant losses to the interests of the State, he shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than three years but not more than seven years and shall also be fined:
"(1) turning over the profitable business of his own unit to his relatives or friends for operation;
"(2) purchasing commodities or accepting services from a unit operated or managed by his relatives or friends at a price obviously higher than the market price, or selling commodities or providing services to a unit operated or managed by his relatives or friends at a price obviously lower than the market price;
"(3) purchasing or accepting substandard commodities or services from a unit operated or managed by his relatives or friends.
"Where a staff member of another company or enterprise, in violation of laws or administrative regulations, commits the act prescribed in the preceding paragraph, thereby causing significant losses to the interests of the company or enterprise, he shall be punished in accordance with the provisions of the preceding paragraph."

5. Article 390 of the Criminal Law is amended to read: "Any person who commits the crime of offering bribes shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years or criminal detention and shall also be fined; if he seeks illegitimate benefits through bribery, with serious circumstances, or causes significant losses to the interests of the State, he shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than three years but not more than ten years and shall also be fined; if the circumstances are especially serious, or if he causes especially significant losses to the interests of the State, he shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than ten years or life imprisonment, and shall also be fined or have his property confiscated.
"Under any of the following circumstances, he shall be given a severe punishment:
"(1) offering bribes on multiple occasions or to multiple persons;
"(2) being a functionary of a State organ and offering bribes;
"(3) offering bribes in relation to a key national project or a major project;
"(4) offering bribes for the purpose of obtaining promotion or adjustment of position or rank;
"(5) offering bribes to a supervisory, administrative law enforcement, or judicial officer;
"(6) offering bribes in the fields of ecological environment, finance, production safety, food and drugs, disaster prevention and relief, social security, education, medical care, etc., and committing illegal or criminal activities;
"(7) using illegally obtained proceeds to offer bribes.
"Where a person who offers bribes voluntarily confesses his bribery before being prosecuted, he may be given a lighter or mitigated punishment. If the crime is minor, or if he plays a key role in breaking through investigations or solving major cases, or if he has performed major meritorious service, he may be given a mitigated punishment or be exempted from punishment."
